{"name":"Snowstorm Space Shuttle","hex":"#001188","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowstorm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Bad weather involving blowing winds and snow, or blowing winds and heavy snowfall amount.","A snow globe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowstorm"},{"term":"space","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Unlimited or generalized extent, physical or otherwise.\nThe distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, walk, wander.","To set some distance apart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space"},{"term":"shuttle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tool used to carry the woof back and forth between the warp threads on a loom.","The sliding thread holder in a sewing machine, which carries the lower thread through a loop of the upper thread, to make a lock stitch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To go or send back and forth between two places.","To transport by shuttle or by means of a shuttle service."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shuttle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Space Shuttle","blocks":[{"text":"The Space Shuttle is a retired, partially reusable low Earth orbital spacecraft system that went to the ISS and performed other orbital missions. Operated from 1981 to 2011 by the U.S. National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) as part of the Space Shuttle program. Its official program name was the Space Transportation System (STS), taken from the 1969 plan led by U.S. vice president Spiro Agnew for a system of reusable spacecraft where it was the only item funded for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/STS120LaunchHiRes-edit1.jpg/330px-STS120LaunchHiRes-edit1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle","wikidata":"Q48806"},{"title":"Winter storm","blocks":[{"text":"A winter storm is an event in which wind coincides with varieties of precipitation that only occur at freezing temperatures, such as snow, mixed snow and rain, or freezing rain. In temperate continental and subarctic climates, these storms are not necessarily restricted to the winter season, but may occur in the late autumn and early spring as well. A snowstorm with strong winds and low visibility is called a blizzard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Winter_Storm_Jonas_2016_NYC_Pershing_Square.jpg/330px-Winter_Storm_Jonas_2016_NYC_Pershing_Square.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_storm","wikidata":"Q75079023"},{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over whether it is itself an entity, a relationship between entities, or part of a conceptual framework."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/3D_coordinate_system.svg/330px-3D_coordinate_system.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space","wikidata":"Q107"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/STS115_Atlantis_undock_ISS_edit2.jpg/500px-STS115_Atlantis_undock_ISS_edit2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/STS115_Atlant